Feature: Calculate Actual Sales Value For Each Brand by Country and Territory

  Background:
    Given the tables purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales and purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales
    And the control table purgo_playground.control_table with valid source_systems

  Scenario: Calculate actual sales value for valid records
    Given a valid brand_name, country_code, and territory_id
    And corresponding sales_month and fiscal_date
    And valid source_system_name exists in the control_table
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should sum sales_value from t3_itm_territory_sales and sales_net_price_local from t3_ttm_territory_sales
    And calculate actual_value for each brand_name, country_code, and territory_id

  Scenario: Ignore records with invalid source_system_name
    Given a brand_name record with source_system_name not in control_table
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should exclude the brand_name record from actual_value calculation

  Scenario Outline: Validate calculation across multiple data points
    Given brand_name "<brand>"
    And country_code "<country>"
    And territory_id "<territory>"
    And sales_month "<sales_month>"
    And fiscal_date "<fiscal_date>"
    And source_system_name "<source_system>"
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should calculate the actual_value correctly if source_system exists in control_table
    Examples:
      | brand    | country | territory | sales_month | fiscal_date | source_system |
      | BrandA   | US      | 101       | 2023-09-01  | 2023-09-01  | SystemA       |
      | BrandB   | UK      | 102       | 2023-09-01  | 2023-09-01  | SystemB       |
      | BrandC   | DE      | 103       | 2023-09-01  | 2023-09-01  | SystemC       |
      | BrandD   | US      | 104       | 2023-09-01  | 2023-09-01  | SystemD       |

  Scenario: Handle error when dates do not align
    Given sales_month is different from fiscal_date for some records
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should flag these records for manual review
    And output error message "Date mismatch: sales_month does not align with fiscal_date"

  Scenario: Ensure proper data format and value handling
    Given sales_value is in decimal format
    And sales_net_price_local is in decimal format
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then ensure actual_value is calculated in decimal format

  Scenario: Exclude records with missing or null fields
    Given a record with null brand_name, country_code, territory_id, or source_system_name
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should exclude this record from actual_value calculation

  Scenario Outline: Verify invalid data scenarios
    Given invalid brand_name "<brand>"
    And country_code "<country>"
    And territory_id "<territory>"
    And source_system_name "<source_system>"
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should not calculate actual_value
    Examples:
      | brand  | country | territory | source_system |
      |        | US      | 105       | SystemE       |
      | BrandE |         | 106       | SystemF       |
      | BrandF | UK      |           | SystemG       |
      | BrandG | DE      | 107       |               |

  Scenario: Check for aggregation grouping
    Given multiple sales values for the same brand_name, country_code, and territory_id
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should group and aggregate correctly to compute the actual_value

  Scenario: Validate data integrity during calculation
    Given valid input data from purgo_playground.t3_itm_territory_sales and purgo_playground.t3_ttm_territory_sales
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then I should maintain data integrity throughout the join and aggregation process

  Scenario: Ensure SQL query follows acceptance criteria
    Given the requirements for calculating actual_value
    And valid data input
    When I execute the SQL query
    Then ensure the output matches expected results and follows acceptance criteria
